//? Title: Naive Bayes: Counts, Absences and Gaussian Features
//? Subtitle: Conditional independence is a model assumption, not a consequence of normalization
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A classifier can combine many weak feature observations through class-conditional likelihoods.
We inspect smoothed multinomial word probabilities and show how Bernoulli likelihoods also count
absent words. A separate Gaussian fixture verifies population variances and a constant-feature
floor. All model state is fitted by explicit tensor Adam loops from the supplied training tensors.
)
\toc

> The method

Naive Bayes uses log score log pi_c + sum_j log p(x_j|c), then softmax-normalises scores.
For multinomial count features with additive smoothing alpha and vocabulary width D,

$$
\theta_{cj}=\frac{\sum_{i:y_i=c}x_{ij}+\alpha}{\sum_j\sum_{i:y_i=c}x_{ij}+\alpha D},\quad
s_c^{\rm Bern}=\log\pi_c+\sum_j[x_j\log\theta_{cj}+(1-x_j)\log(1-\theta_{cj})].
$$
\alttext(Multinomial probabilities normalise smoothed word counts; Bernoulli log likelihood includes both present and absent features.)

Multinomial scores omit the query's class-independent factorial coefficient, which does not
change posteriors. An empty count document therefore reduces to the class prior. An all-zero
Bernoulli document still contributes absence probabilities. Gaussian features use per-class
population variance with an absolute positive floor. Every class must occur in training;
callers supply valid nonnegative counts or binary indicators. The absolute variance constraint is specified in feature-squared units.
The visible loops optimise the supervised generative joint likelihood, not discriminative
cross-entropy of the class posterior. Initial and conditional logits remain learnable leaves.
Multinomial pseudocounts add alpha times the sum of log conditional word probabilities;
Bernoulli adds alpha times log p plus log(1-p) for every feature. Their stationary points
are exactly the displayed smoothed count formulas. The empirical prior maximises the
label likelihood. Gaussian Adam fits means and log variances; after each update, an
explicit projection enforces variance at least .001. Fitting is iterative, not a constructor
side effect. Each full-batch iteration and prediction costs O(ND) and O(QKD), respectively.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/naive_bayes_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/naive_bayes_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/naive_bayes_concept.tikz > build/naive_bayes_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/naive_bayes_concept.svg build/naive_bayes_concept.dvi > build/naive_bayes_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/naive_bayes_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
